# A client alone: connect, write, read, flush and close, with no listener in
# the program. A Conn in the program loads every Conn native, since its
# declared Reader/Writer conformance takes their addresses; nothing of the
# Listener is loaded. Whether a server happens to listen on the port does not
# matter: both arms print the same line.
main: function is {
    cr: net.connect port: 49331
    match (
        cr
    ) case ok then {
        msg: Bytes
        msg.append from: 1.u8
        bv: msg.byteView
        w: cr.write from: bv
        buf: Bytes
        r: cr.read into: buf max: 4
        f: cr.flush
        c: cr.close
        print "client done"
    } case err then {
        print "client done"
    }
}
